        <p>A fashion C 4 toque suitable for • young matron ire formed . ect pee:lett. and trimmed with holly- hock. and pink velvet. Some of the new toques are rather large, and the majority of them are decidedly pretty end becoming, although some in- cline to scoentrecety. A charming epecimen of the aimpler kind ho • crown of cream Japanem Straw, and ain composed of sine!' bunch. of erismilipe and rosette@ of cream lace, while ire front a bunch ed the yellow flowers rums from the centre of • mide double-looped buw made of gauze-edged chine ribbon of two kinds, toe having a pattern in delicate shades of green on • cream ground, the other being plain green with a line of rom•colour in the border. A similar and equally pretty wpm km mauve primula@ in place of the violets, and loops of efeep purple velvet or,- substituted for those of green and pink ribbon. Very fashionalele are toques of jotted net, with high sheaf-bown of fancy ribbon at the end., and brims made of ruches of chiffon and dowers aunt-Ma, °tenor, and violet. being among the most }eviller bloirsonn at the time of writigs,</p>
